              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Lvolve"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Made this per recipe. Then needed more and did not want more SC or Mayo as 1/2 C seems a plenty. So. \nI just doubled ingredients added chicken broth and poured on the fish as it broiled. Did not actually use the SC version and was so tasty with the chicken broth.",
            "datePublished": "2020-04-17T20:22:07.143Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "OkinawanPrincess"
            },
            "reviewBody": "very nice dill sauce. Because I was only making for two people I sclaed it down a bit. I also added a little mayonnaise because it seemed to be something and I also added teeny pinch of sugar. I mixed it well and let it marinate overnight. This goes well with grilled salmon or any fish dish.",
            "datePublished": "2011-06-11T13:56:40.780Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Joanne O"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I used sour cream and just a dollop of Mayo. Increased the dill &amp; mustard. I also use this as a “base recipe” for dips by changing up the herbs. I’ve substituted dill for tarragon for chicken cordon blue sauce. Delish and so easy!",
            "datePublished": "2021-05-23T17:07:28.833Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "JumpySalt2768"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Very good. I followed the suggestion to add some kosher salt and pepper, and a bit more lemon juice - I squeezed half of a large lemon so it was probably around 2 Tbsp. Letting it sit in the fridge is key - everything melds nicely. If I have fresh chives I add some, finely chopped.",
            "datePublished": "2022-10-15T19:53:32.632Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Geri Chance"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I added a touch more lemon juice and Dijon mustard and dill (all I had was dry dill). It is fabulous! Even on veggies!",
            "datePublished": "2020-05-05T23:40:00.653Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Socal Sue"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I will make it again. I added salt and pepper and let set in the fridge for a couple of hours. It was much better the next day.",
            "datePublished": "2019-10-23T01:30:04.443Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Nunez triO"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Very easy. substitued the 1 cup of sour cream for 3/4 mayo &amp; 1/4 cream cheese. And used McCormick dill. \nLove the alternations possiblity",
            "datePublished": "2020-04-29T16:00:38.703Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "masdevallia"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This was really tasty. I subbed NF yogurt for 1/2 of the sour cream and whole grain mustard for dijon. It was great! I found this just before serving salmon fishcakes (Nigella Lawson) so didn't have time to let it chill as directed. After dinner, I tasted the sauce again. It was definitely better for the sitting time. I'll be sure to make it ahead next time so the flavors can meld before serving.",
            "datePublished": "2011-04-28T21:12:28.157Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "reisi"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This is a great sauce! I also added mayonnaise and upped the amount of dill. When I poach the fish I also add some of the poaching liquid to the sauce to thin it out a little bit. Adds flavour, too!",
            "datePublished": "2013-04-12T15:47:25.723Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Laura Dayok"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I added a little mayo and used dried dill because I didn't have fresh. This reminded me a lot of a sauce my grandma use to make for salmon when I was a kid. However, she would peel and de-seed a cucumber, chop it into small pieces and add it with the sauce. I didn't do that this time because I wanted to see how the original turned out, but I am going to add the cucumber in next time out of nostalgia.",
            "datePublished": "2019-02-04T17:08:25.937Z"
          },
          {
